cachetrace
==========

This project is a derivative work built on top of http-cache-semantics.

Upstream
--------
  Project : http-cache-semantics
  Author  : Kornel Lesiński
  Source  : https://github.com/kornelski/http-cache-semantics
  Version : 4.3.0 (decision semantics aligned with this release)
  Commit  : b1d4bd682fbab0252985de45219f4e7497c0067c
  License : BSD-2-Clause

What cachetrace adds
--------------------
cachetrace does not vendor or modify upstream source code. It consumes upstream
as a peer dependency at runtime and provides an explainability layer on top:

  - an independent replay of the same decision rules, emitting a node per check
  - differential verification of that replay against upstream, per request
  - counterfactual analysis whose every suggestion is re-verified upstream
  - batch auditing over HAR / NDJSON / JSON response inventories

Upstream's own test suite is not modified and continues to pass unchanged.
The BSD-2-Clause text in LICENSE covers both the upstream portions and the
cachetrace additions.

Specification references
------------------------
RFC 9111 (HTTP Caching), RFC 7234 (obsoleted predecessor), RFC 5861
(stale-while-revalidate / stale-if-error), RFC 7231 §6.1 (cacheable status codes).
